## 2. Model Overview

The SIMULINK model used in this tutorial was originally developed by **Professor Rodney Tan**. The frequency relay block is **not available in the standard MATLAB SIMULINK library** — it is a custom block created by Prof. Rodney Tan.

### Key Blocks in the Model

| Block | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **Three-Phase Programmable Voltage Source** | Generates the supply voltage with frequency variation |
| **Three-Phase Measurement (Bus A & Bus B)** | Measures phase voltage at two buses |
| **Three-Phase Series RLC Load** | Two loads connected at Bus A and Bus B |
| **Scopes (A & B)** | Display voltage waveforms at Bus A and Bus B |
| **Frequency Relay Block (81)** | The main protection block (custom-built) |
| **Circuit Breaker** | Disconnects the load when trip signal is received |

---

## 3. Step-by-Step Design Process

### Step 1: Three-Phase Programmable Voltage Source
- **Positive sequence voltage amplitude:** 400 V (phase-to-phase line voltage)
- **Angle:** 0°
- **Frequency:** 50 Hz
- **Time variation:** Frequency (selected)
- **Type of variation:** Step function
- **Step magnitude:** -3 Hz (for under frequency test) → frequency drops to **47 Hz**
- **Time variation:** Starts at **0.1 s**, ends at **0.8 s**

### Step 2: Three-Phase Measurement Blocks
- Named **Bus A** and **Bus B**
- Measure **phase-to-ground** voltage

### Step 3: Three-Phase Series RLC Load
- Two loads connected at Bus A and Bus B
- Same parameter values (400 V, other values chosen randomly)
- **Load at Bus B is critical** → Under frequency relay is applied here to disconnect it during low frequency

### Step 4: Frequency Relay Block (81)
- **System frequency:** 50 Hz (can be changed to 60 Hz)
- **Under/Over frequency setting:** 5% by default (range: 1% to 20%)
  - 1% = 0.5 Hz variation
  - 5% = 2.5 Hz variation → relay operates when frequency goes below **47.5 Hz**
- **Ride through time delay:** 0.2 seconds (time for relay + breaker to disconnect load)

#### Inside the Frequency Relay Block (Subsystem)
- **PLL (Phase Locked Loop):** Measures frequency
- **MATLAB Function Block:** Implements the frequency relay logic
  - Inputs: frequency, limits, time delay
  - Output: Trip signal (TS)
  - Adds **20 ms delay** to simulate mechanical relay movement time
- **Clock** and **Scope** for frequency measurement

### Step 5: Circuit Breaker
- All three phases initially **closed**
- **Switching time:** External (waits for trip signal from frequency relay)

